	(text "HC-RJ45-059D-2x8-2-04: one 2x8 ganged block, 16 jacks, NO MAGNETICS (8 signal pins per jack).\nPinout is Cisco \"Console Port Mode 2\" (rolled in the PCB): 3 = RxD in, 6 = TxD out, 4/5 = GND, 1/2/7/8 open.\nStraight-through Cat5 patch cables work; no blue rollover cable needed.\nColumn j (0..7, left to right): P(2j+1) = lower jack, pads 24j+1..8;  P(2j+2) = upper jack, pads 24j+9..16.\nThe upper jack is inverted and numbered the other way - VERIFY with a 3-6 loopback on one upper and one lower\njack at bring-up. A mistake here gives eight silently dead ports that no ERC/DRC catches."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "190e81de-949e-54c5-8c7b-2cfa9619d0f8")
	)
	(text "TP: scope ground near the jacks"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 158 259 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2328c069-33b0-5f1b-b01d-020e13f023ac")
	)
	(text "SHIELD: all 16 shells common through the frame, one connection point.\nFootprint set 0R / high-value R / C - 0R fitted. Keeps the option to break the\nsixteen parallel ground paths that shielded patch cables would otherwise create."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 90 225 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
